[
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "PRODUCT DESIGN CASE STUDY",
  "x": 168,
  "y": 40,
  "w": 191,
  "h": 14,
  "size": "12px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "FA",
  "x": 293,
  "y": 64,
  "w": 22,
  "h": 19,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "900"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Read in Persian:",
  "x": 168,
  "y": 69,
  "w": 97,
  "h": 14,
  "size": "12px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Why Didn't Our Educational Game Feel Like a Game?",
  "x": 168,
  "y": 124,
  "w": 855,
  "h": 38,
  "size": "32px",
  "weight": "700"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "The story of a game that had everything, except a way in.",
  "x": 168,
  "y": 190,
  "w": 800,
  "h": 29,
  "size": "24px",
  "weight": "500"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Role: Product Designer | Timeline: 4 weeks | Tools: Figma, Illustrator, Pen & Paper | Product: Classeh",
  "x": 168,
  "y": 259,
  "w": 821,
  "h": 19,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "Ke9G0xrwBgaY5bDWEnaMXL85FZQ.png",
  "x": 168,
  "y": 318,
  "w": 944,
  "h": 465
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "CONTEXT",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 863,
  "w": 67,
  "h": 17,
  "size": "14px",
  "weight": "500"
 },
 {
  "type": "h3",
  "text": "Live, and ready to grow",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 896,
  "w": 943,
  "h": 34,
  "size": "28px",
  "weight": "700"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "By the time I joined, Classeh's educational game was already live, sold to schools, stocked with content, doing its job. It wasn't broken. I",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 945,
  "w": 943,
  "h": 51,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "The brief was simple to say and open to everything: make it better. No one had a diagnosis yet, that part was on me to find.",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 1011,
  "w": 943,
  "h": 51,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "DeeysiCw3wyZVikupZ9aQkx3eE.png",
  "x": 170,
  "y": 1102,
  "w": 171,
  "h": 297
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "ndR1Ra8IyTEFVqD3r6x9xWwHrU.png",
  "x": 343,
  "y": 1219,
  "w": 770,
  "h": 120
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "BEFORE",
  "x": 609,
  "y": 1407,
  "w": 62,
  "h": 19,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "700"
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "91EBCjBAA8QL72F7Zuu5AcRiB8M.png",
  "x": 351,
  "y": 1466,
  "w": 770,
  "h": 151
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "jhJb8xdrdg5x0vkjJGadQtX3pc.png",
  "x": 160,
  "y": 1469,
  "w": 272,
  "h": 193
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "AFTER",
  "x": 614,
  "y": 1670,
  "w": 52,
  "h": 19,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "700"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "PROBLEM STATEMENT",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 1769,
  "w": 148,
  "h": 17,
  "size": "14px",
  "weight": "500"
 },
 {
  "type": "h3",
  "text": "A Game? Or a Table of Contents?",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 1802,
  "w": 943,
  "h": 34,
  "size": "28px",
  "weight": "700"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Getting to a single game meant three separate decisions, made correctly, in order: subject, then chapter, then finally a list of games to ch",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 1852,
  "w": 943,
  "h": 51,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "That's not a game flow. That's a table of contents.",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 1917,
  "w": 943,
  "h": 26,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "The navigation had been built around how a curriculum is structured — not around how a kid decides what to play next. And every one of those",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 1956,
  "w": 943,
  "h": 51,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "2QaeCqwqOaupzyWXynrNpMPNEGo.png",
  "x": 330,
  "y": 2089,
  "w": 180,
  "h": 390
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "Vs0g4FzQbBbpPlQbzdq7cWcuDM.png",
  "x": 550,
  "y": 2089,
  "w": 180,
  "h": 390
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "N2EbeWAiT9yq8p1oqjCsVG18lCQ.png",
  "x": 770,
  "y": 2089,
  "w": 180,
  "h": 390
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "The previous flow: subject, then chapter, then a list of games. and only then, a game.",
  "x": 308,
  "y": 2519,
  "w": 664,
  "h": 19,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "EVALUATION & RESEARCH",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 2778,
  "w": 178,
  "h": 17,
  "size": "14px",
  "weight": "500"
 },
 {
  "type": "h3",
  "text": "Chasing Clues",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 2811,
  "w": 943,
  "h": 34,
  "size": "28px",
  "weight": "700"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Research wasn't yet a standard part of the process there, so I pulled together whatever signal I could get on my own.",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 2860,
  "w": 943,
  "h": 26,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "I ran a lightweight heuristic evaluation against the existing flow, then handed the game to a few teenagers I knew -also part of our target ",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 2900,
  "w": 943,
  "h": 77,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Clarity's session recordings backed up what I was seeing live: kids lingering on the same screen far longer than a two-second menu should ta",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 2991,
  "w": 943,
  "h": 77,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "eV40b9PYueHtbOpSSv8wKtM966Q.png",
  "x": 512,
  "y": 3089,
  "w": 271,
  "h": 291
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "piw1xroDsADkLF37F7RmuA8skwQ.png",
  "x": 742,
  "y": 3102,
  "w": 265,
  "h": 265
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "RSm2YT3zaFjJBOVlOXdrTxizYlA.png",
  "x": 272,
  "y": 3110,
  "w": 272,
  "h": 248
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Two things kept surfacing:",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 3401,
  "w": 943,
  "h": 26,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "— No intuitive flow: the path to play was a sequence of independent decisions, made correctly, in order, with no sense of progress in betwee",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 3441,
  "w": 943,
  "h": 51,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "— Inconsistent visual language: pieces of the product didn't feel like they belonged together, which worked against the sense of immersion w",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 3506,
  "w": 943,
  "h": 51,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "hnzZn8iaJvI6DsIR5pU4465lOAY.png",
  "x": 440,
  "y": 3578,
  "w": 400,
  "h": 192
 },
 {
  "type": "h6",
  "text": "COMPETITIVE ANALYSIS",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 3850,
  "w": 161,
  "h": 17,
  "size": "14px",
  "weight": "500"
 },
 {
  "type": "h3",
  "text": "The App Should've Thought Ahead",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 3883,
  "w": 943,
  "h": 34,
  "size": "28px",
  "weight": "700"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "I looked at three educational apps to see how they handle the same tension:",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 3933,
  "w": 943,
  "h": 26,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "content that needs structure, but still has to feel like play.",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 3972,
  "w": 943,
  "h": 26,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "The pattern across the two most game-like products was clear: the app should already know what a user is doing next. Every time we made kids",
  "x": 169,
  "y": 4012,
  "w": 943,
  "h": 51,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "bZaEPXxujLMIpMDmxyq2xsnTfws.png",
  "x": 173,
  "y": 4126,
  "w": 32,
  "h": 32
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Duolingo",
  "x": 215,
  "y": 4130,
  "w": 92,
  "h": 24,
  "size": "20px",
  "weight": "700"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Levels are gated, no skipping ahead without clearing what came before.",
  "x": 173,
  "y": 4182,
  "w": 934,
  "h": 26,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Open the app, and it already knows your next step.",
  "x": 173,
  "y": 4222,
  "w": 934,
  "h": 26,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "No need to remember where you were, it just picks up for you.",
  "x": 173,
  "y": 4261,
  "w": 934,
  "h": 26,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "t9I9YKRE7Q7wojx4yD21dOyNW1g.png",
  "x": 371,
  "y": 4367,
  "w": 539,
  "h": 503
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "N9mJa9RtgA31VdN2kqXT4t5LM.webp",
  "x": 173,
  "y": 4933,
  "w": 32,
  "h": 32
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Bussu",
  "x": 215,
  "y": 4937,
  "w": 61,
  "h": 24,
  "size": "20px",
  "weight": "700"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Units instead of levels, same idea: pick up right where you left off.",
  "x": 173,
  "y": 4981,
  "w": 934,
  "h": 26,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "5P4OJKhxPVo00ld0wym98ECU7U.png",
  "x": 361,
  "y": 5086,
  "w": 558,
  "h": 503
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "ZoImJxweDnOECoKM2ZjtERU6MI.webp",
  "x": 173,
  "y": 5652,
  "w": 32,
  "h": 32
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Khan academy kids",
  "x": 215,
  "y": 5656,
  "w": 206,
  "h": 24,
  "size": "20px",
  "weight": "700"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Every game sits visible at once, no category steps stand between the user and what they want to play. Categories are still there, just as a ",
  "x": 173,
  "y": 5700,
  "w": 934,
  "h": 51,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "cyJH6ZWGX6XzreHGUXQN2NBRaM.png",
  "x": 361,
  "y": 5772,
  "w": 558,
  "h": 569
 },
 {
  "type": "h6",
  "text": "HMW",
  "x": 168,
  "y": 6581,
  "w": 36,
  "h": 17,
  "size": "14px",
  "weight": "500"
 },
 {
  "type": "h3",
  "text": "Finding the Right Question",
  "x": 168,
  "y": 6613,
  "w": 944,
  "h": 34,
  "size": "28px",
  "weight": "700"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Discovery had pointed to a clear cause, The next step was turning that into a question I could actually design against:",
  "x": 168,
  "y": 6663,
  "w": 918,
  "h": 26,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "How might we make the navigation experience simpler and more familiar, aligning with users' mental model?",
  "x": 188,
  "y": 6721,
  "w": 924,
  "h": 70,
  "size": "22px",
  "weight": "500"
 },
 {
  "type": "h6",
  "text": "USER FLOW",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 6873,
  "w": 77,
  "h": 17,
  "size": "14px",
  "weight": "500"
 },
 {
  "type": "h3",
  "text": "Cutting the Decision, Not Simplifying It",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 6905,
  "w": 939,
  "h": 34,
  "size": "28px",
  "weight": "700"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Mapping the existing flow end-to-end surfaced something I hadn't expected:",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 6955,
  "w": 939,
  "h": 26,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "this three-step decision sequence wasn't a one-time hurdle. It repeated multiple times in a single play session — and each repetition risked",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 6995,
  "w": 939,
  "h": 51,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "The fix wasn't to make each decision easier. It was to remove the repeated decision-making altogether.",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 7060,
  "w": 939,
  "h": 26,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "I restructured the flow into a single, continuous path. Instead of subject → chapter → game list as three separate choices, progress became ",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 7099,
  "w": 939,
  "h": 51,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "To make the difference visible, I marked the actual game — the point of play — with a star (⭐) in both diagrams. In the old flow, that star ",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 7165,
  "w": 939,
  "h": 51,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "BEFORE",
  "x": 609,
  "y": 7298,
  "w": 62,
  "h": 19,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "700"
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "ndR1Ra8IyTEFVqD3r6x9xWwHrU.png",
  "x": 255,
  "y": 7341,
  "w": 770,
  "h": 120
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "The star marks the game itself — reached only after a three-step branching path.",
  "x": 322,
  "y": 7485,
  "w": 636,
  "h": 19,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "AFTER",
  "x": 614,
  "y": 7624,
  "w": 52,
  "h": 19,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "700"
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "91EBCjBAA8QL72F7Zuu5AcRiB8M.png",
  "x": 255,
  "y": 7667,
  "w": 770,
  "h": 151
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Same star, same game — now just one step away.",
  "x": 447,
  "y": 7842,
  "w": 387,
  "h": 19,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Key improvements over the previous flow:",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 8094,
  "w": 939,
  "h": 26,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "h6",
  "text": "SKETCH",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 8128,
  "w": 54,
  "h": 17,
  "size": "14px",
  "weight": "500"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "→ Clear overview: users can now see everything relevant to their current progress in a single glance",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 8133,
  "w": 939,
  "h": 26,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "h3",
  "text": "Starting With Pen and Paper",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 8161,
  "w": 939,
  "h": 34,
  "size": "28px",
  "weight": "700"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "→ Seamless progression: finishing a step reveals the next one automatically — no manual navigating required",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 8173,
  "w": 939,
  "h": 26,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Early hand-drawn sketches of the screens the new flow would require, before any high-fidelity design.",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 8211,
  "w": 939,
  "h": 26,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "biCTfqDK6ihy1mNmO2xKlkMxktQ.png",
  "x": 284,
  "y": 8276,
  "w": 712,
  "h": 439
 },
 {
  "type": "h6",
  "text": "INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 8795,
  "w": 209,
  "h": 17,
  "size": "14px",
  "weight": "500"
 },
 {
  "type": "h3",
  "text": "Stepping on Backend's Turf",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 8828,
  "w": 939,
  "h": 34,
  "size": "28px",
  "weight": "700"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "The new flow needed a content structure to match. Different books had different numbers of lessons, and different content within them — so a",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 8878,
  "w": 939,
  "h": 77,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "My first instinct was to distribute content around the school's actual curriculum schedule, rather than how lessons happened to be grouped. ",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 8968,
  "w": 939,
  "h": 77,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "I brought it to our CTO expecting pushback, or at best a scaled-down compromise. Instead, he told me to go ahead.",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 9059,
  "w": 939,
  "h": 26,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "That green light was what turned this from a UI exercise into a real structural project — and it's what let me take the idea from a rough di",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 9099,
  "w": 939,
  "h": 128,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "h6",
  "text": "VISIUAL IDENTITY",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 9467,
  "w": 117,
  "h": 17,
  "size": "14px",
  "weight": "500"
 },
 {
  "type": "h3",
  "text": "Beezie Takes the Stage",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 9500,
  "w": 939,
  "h": 34,
  "size": "28px",
  "weight": "700"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Beezie wasn't something I inherited — it's something I proposed adding to the game myself, and the work of bringing it to life was assigned ",
  "x": 171,
  "y": 9549,
  "w": 939,
  "h": 77,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "img",
  "file": "P21Kr54EdcC7XqEY5bY2jZ6w.png",
  "x": 339,
  "y": 9664,
  "w": 602,
  "h": 205
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Beezie, Classe's mascot.",
  "x": 546,
  "y": 9879,
  "w": 188,
  "h": 19,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
 {
  "type": "p",
  "text": "Once the new roadmap structure was in place, the work went beyond the mascot itself. I designed the visual elements for each of the eight se",
  "x": 172,
  "y": 9978,
  "w": 937,
  "h": 77,
  "size": "16px",
  "weight": "400"
 },
